{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4lfdzq7nblyf2p5dbcte4rd3o3dhjh65um5vvq52p4lhmqe7t42a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is byte-exact; no source fixes were needed.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ symbol diff empty; C exports exactly one symbol (`tfm`), Rust exports it. `RTLD_NOW` dlopen succeeds |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row passes on randomized inputs | ✅ 26/26 rows |\n| C/Rust binary stdout match | ✅ vacuous — no `add_executable` in CMakeLists, no `[[bin]]` |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing test | ✅ 17/17 rows + 3 generic-boundary tests |\n| Holds under every feature combination | ✅ no `[features]` declared; all 4 configs (default/`--no-default-features` × debug/release) pass 52/52 |\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `verify.sh` (driver: builds C, enumerates configs, symbol-diffs, runs all phases, optional `mutate` gate), and `tests/{common/mod.rs, phase_a_harness.rs, phase_b_valid.rs, phase_c_errors.rs, phase_d_parity.rs}` — 2780 lines. Both `.so`s are always loaded via `libloading` and called through `dlsym(\"tfm\")`.\n\n## Findings worth flagging\n\n1. **Negative discriminant is genuinely reachable.** Though `(dy2-dx2)²+4dxy²` is mathematically ≥0, the C computes it *expanded*, so cancellation makes it negative for ~25% of near-equal inputs. The `(0 > sqd) ? 0 : sqd` clamp is a live path, not dead code — covered by `row07` / `err09`.\n\n2. **`sqd == -0.0` is unreachable** (the `+4*dxy*dxy` addend is `+0.0` for all finite `dxy`, and `x + (+0.0)` is never `-0.0`). `ERRORS.md` row 10 was corrected to target the reachable `+0.0` boundary instead.\n\n3. **`fsqrt`'s negative-argument branch is provably dead** (the clamp guarantees `x >= 0`, `-0.0`, or NaN), matching the C where `comiss/jbe` substitutes the `0.0f` constant before `sqrtf@plt`, so `errno` is never set. Excluded from mutation testing with justification rather than reported as a coverage gap.\n\n4. **The C library disagrees with itself across `-O` levels** — confirming `lib.rs`'s doc comment. Over 60M random triples, `gcc -O2` diverges from the CMake build on 7,573 inputs and `-O3` on 4,242 — **but every divergence requires a NaN *input operand*; zero on NaN-free input.** The Rust matches the build `CMakeLists.txt` actually produces (`-O0`) on all 60M inputs in both profiles. Pinned by a permanent test that rebuilds the C at each `-O` level.\n\n5. **Harness validated by mutation testing**: 19 planted bugs (operand-order commutation, NaN-payload selection rules, `INDEFINITE` sign bit, 1-ulp coefficient perturbations, stride/loop-guard/signedness errors, f64 intermediates) — all 19 caught. Two initially \"uncaught\" results were diagnosed: one mutation rounded back to the identical `f32` (fixed to a true 1-ulp perturbation), the other targeted the dead branch above.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (checksums verified); only `c_src/build/` was added by cmake."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":613,"cache_read_input_tokens":134107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":613,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d9b716-85f9-4088-b8c7-7e0e7bf70850","uuid":"4ee76077-3e39-4634-a4b4-6ea2c0b789d8","timestamp":"2026-09-05T02:28:01.793Z"}
